--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party validation artefacts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The published npm packages contain PRECOMPILED (SEF) forms of third-party
validation artefacts. Those files are not covered by Apache 2.0; they keep the
licence of their source:

1. eInvoicing-EN16931 validation artefacts — CEN/TC 434
   Licence: EUPL 1.2
   Source:  https://github.com/ConnectingEurope/eInvoicing-EN16931
   Version: validation-1.3.16
   Shipped in `verifaktura` as sef/en16931-ubl.sef.json and sef/en16931-cii.sef.json

2. Specifikacija osnovne uporabe eRačuna s proširenjima (Croatian CIUS)
   Source:  Ministarstvo financija — Porezna uprava Republike Hrvatske
            https://porezna.gov.hr/fiskalizacija/bezgotovinski-racuni/eracun
   Terms:   the content may be redistributed without special permission,
            provided the source is credited
   Shipped in `@verifaktura/cius-hr` as sef/hr-cius-ext-ubl.sef.json

3. ISO Schematron skeleton (build-time tool, not shipped in any package)
   Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2004-2010 Rick Jelliffe and Academia Sinica
   Source:  https://github.com/schematron/schematron

This repository contains none of these artefacts — they are downloaded by
`npm run prepare:sef` and packaged only at publish time, so that validation
never runs against stale rules.

English rule texts are the original texts of the sources listed above.
Translations into Croatian, Bosnian and Serbian are the work of this project and
are licensed under Apache 2.0.
